        "subject": "feat(boundary): HISO-005 BUILD0244 ESM module shape in the B6 kernel (star re-export, refused class)",
        "body": "feat(boundary): HISO-005 BUILD0244 ESM module shape in the B6 kernel (star re-export, refused class)\n\nSPEC0244 E1/E2 (docs/02_spec/0244_b6_esm_module_shape.md, approved by the\nuser for a local BUILD), on top of the PR #8 head (BUILD0243/0242).\n\n- E1: `export * from` and `export * as ns from` follow the ECMAScript module\n  semantics when the source is an analysed ESM module with a complete\n  namespace (not CommonJS, contained, a cycle or U). Every export name keeps\n  its resolved binding (module#local through indirect exports and stars).\n  Different bindings make a name ambiguous: U with UNKNOWN_REEXPORT\n  AMBIGUOUS_STAR:<name>, sticky, and propagated to every star re-exporter.\n  Explicit runtime exports prevail wherever they stand; type-only and ambient\n  exports never mask; `default` is never re-exported. A module with any\n  non-qualified star keeps UNKNOWN_REEXPORT, its star names become U and its\n  namespace is incomplete (transitively). A re-exported namespace is a\n  binding of the re-exporting module, as in the pinned Node 22.\n- E2: a ClassDeclaration keeps its UNKNOWN_UNSUPPORTED_SYNTAX root and its\n  body is never analysed; the name is predeclared U at block entry (TDZ) and\n  exported as U (named, default, anonymous default); `declare class` also\n  yields UNKNOWN_RUNTIME_DECLARATION.\n- The refusal census keeps the v4 behaviour. Limits, profile, recipes and the\n  global proof rule are unchanged. Kernel version\n  semantic-kernel-v5-esm-module-shape.\n\nThe kernel version literal is migrated in four B6 tests, as registered in the\ncontract. New test tests/b6-0244-esm-module-shape.test.js (50 cases). On the\nevaluated root 228e7918 the B6 measurement goes from 13,521 to 12,283\ndiagnostics. The SPEC0244 section 3.3 conservation passes tuple by tuple in\nnormal and strict, with 0 proofs and 0 violations. B6 stays INCOMPLETE.\n\nFresh critic: R1 and R2 REVISE. Every finding was fixed; R2-01 was fixed\nafter the two-round budget, without a third round. Focal 872/872 and native\nprofile 79/79 ran on the frozen bytes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "Ricardo Akinaga",
          "email": "245769618+ricardoakinaga-dev@users.noreply.github.com",
          "time": 1792470776000
